{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPaZ8TM6nhVswCdKcA5K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the three hidden pod-side commands (`job-pre`, `job-exec`, `job-post`) as separate packages, wired into `cmd/ard/main.go`, plus the CLI flags and a `CheckoutTree` method in gitx. The tests I ran pass. A full `go test ./...` timed out at 2 minutes in this sandbox, so it never finished.\n\nWhat I ran and saw pass:\n- **Build and vet:** `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/jobexec`.\n- **Tests:** gitx, cli, jobpre, jobexec, jobpost, docscheck, effects and cmd.\n\nThings a reviewer should know:\n- **Auth header:** `jobpod` doesn't define one, so `job-post` expects `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. The #317 client has to send the same.\n- **Orphan reaping:** it runs only on Linux and only when job-exec is PID 1, so the unit tests can't cover it. The kind-based test in #321 is the real check.\n- **Container restart:** `job-exec` fails if `/job/home/.claude` already exists, so the pod should not restart that container.\n- **Checked on Linux, not Windows:** the Linux build of `jobexec` passed `go vet`. The non-unix build was not vetted, because `GOOS=windows go vet` stopped on a dependency download.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/316/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":85447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"output_tokens":491,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5ecbafa-7392-4828-b470-c1e3cfd37892","uuid":"b48381c7-9cb4-4cab-9c58-3925a665d207","timestamp":"2026-11-25T11:37:29.237Z","request_id":"req_011ChPaZ8CUNYRuv6nG6752q"}
